Validation evidence: make credential-free-validate LEGACY_ROOT=/Users/iv/Developer/relux-proxy exited 0. It passed relay bootstrap, deterministic generation, macOS Debug/Release host and provider builds/contracts, Core boundaries, 443 Swift tests in 37 suites with 25 intentional known issues, Swift Release build, native packaging, relay smoke, and legacy preservation/negative tests/Swift test/Release build. git diff --check, sh -n, and ShellCheck each exited 0. Production signing and deferred iOS were correctly reported NOT RUN.

Required rework 1: scripts/validate-workspace-foundation.sh lines 38-47 use non-exact grep -F for required schemes. A fabricated six-scheme list omitting ReluxProxyMac, retaining ReluxProxyMacTunnel, and adding UnexpectedScheme satisfies the current count and every required-scheme assertion with exit 0. This violates AC2 for missing or unexpected schemes. Compare the exact normalized scheme set or use exact-line checks that cannot alias ReluxProxyMac to ReluxProxyMacTunnel, and add a regression test for both missing and unexpected schemes.

Required rework 2: .github/workflows/ci.yml invokes the local gate on macos-15 without provisioning Mise, while scripts/validate-credential-free.sh requires mise and generate-workspace.sh uses it to install pinned Tuist. GitHub runner-images macos-15 inventory contains neither Mise nor Tuist: https://github.com/actions/runner-images/blob/main/images/macos/macos-15-Readme.md . A clean GitHub runner therefore has no defined bootstrap path to the single entry point, violating AC1 and AC5. Add a checksum/version-pinned credential-free Mise setup before invoking the unchanged policy entry point, or replace the prerequisite with a repository-owned pinned bootstrap, and validate that workflow contract.

Architecture fit is otherwise sound: macOS-only graph and explicit deferred-iOS absence match ADR-024/ADR-027. Tests currently pass, but the missing negative coverage and CI bootstrap prevent acceptance.
